{
    "patcher": {
        "fileversion": 1,
        "appversion": {
            "major": 9,
            "minor": 1,
            "revision": 4,
            "architecture": "x64",
            "modernui": 1
        },
        "classnamespace": "box",
        "rect": [ 85.0, 104.0, 1000.0, 640.0 ],
        "description": "_br.shaper.example.1.1 -- Created by Brian Riordan, guaguanco127@gmail.com -- https://github.com/guaguanco127/ -- Credits: antiderivative anti-aliasing (Parker, Zavalishin & Le Bivic, \"Reducing the Aliasing of Nonlinear Waveshaping Using Continuous-Time Convolution\", DAFx-16, 2016); the buchla shape is in the style of the Buchla 259 timbre circuit.",
        "showrootpatcherontab": 0,
        "showontab": 0,
        "boxes": [
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-signature",
                    "linecount": 5,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 1051.0, 15.0, 520.0, 74.0 ],
                    "text": "_br.shaper.example.1.1 -- Created by Brian Riordan, guaguanco127@gmail.com\nhttps://github.com/guaguanco127/\nCredits: antiderivative anti-aliasing (Parker, Zavalishin & Le Bivic, \"Reducing the Aliasing of Nonlinear Waveshaping Using Continuous-Time Convolution\", DAFx-16, 2016); the buchla shape is in the style of the Buchla 259 timbre circuit."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-1",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 15.0, 79.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "br.shaper"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-2",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 40.0, 760.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "Mono waveshapers in gen~ for synthesis: fold, wrap, clip and buchla (sine fold), one abstraction each, plus br.shaper.multi with all four."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "linecount": 4,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 65.0, 674.0, 60.0 ],
                    "text": "Two files per shape. br.shaper.<shape>.ui.1.1 has dials and a State outlet: load it in a [bpatcher]. br.shaper.<shape>.1.1 is the plain object with no dials: Drive and Mix (and multi's Mode) go straight into gen~, so they take numbers or signals (see the plain object and lfo tabs). Every file has the inlets Input, Drive, Mix (multi adds Mode). Hover an inlet for its range and default."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-4",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 130.0, 1006.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "Antialiased (1st-order ADAA), so high drive doesn't fill the spectrum with aliasing. Drive and Mix glide 10 ms; multi's Mode crossfades 20 ms. No DC filter, so LFOs pass through untouched."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-5",
                    "linecount": 6,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 160.0, 520.0, 87.0 ],
                    "text": "Tabs:\n  multi: all four in one, with the Mode menu\n  singles: the four shapers side by side, with a listen menu\n  lfo: a slow sine shaped by multi; the plain multi with an LFO on Drive\n  plain object: the five plain objects on audio, one LFO sweeping Drive\n  State outlet: reading multi's State outlet by name"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-6",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 255.0, 600.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "Outputs start muted at -70 dB: turn on audio, then raise the slider slowly."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-7",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 15.0, 280.0, 303.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "By Brian Riordan. github.com/guaguanco127"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
